    <briefdescription>
<para>Resolves stack frame addresses to frame keys. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>A frame key is an identifier from the name of the symbol of the address. When the image has no symbol for the address, the key comes from the name of the image. When the address has no image, the key is not valid. The object keeps each key that it made, so each address resolves one time. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
